9126,7.00831832267405098331268367180092027,30.9001801279113882002477959383889572\\r\\nrescue_bound_optional_equity_price_208.40,e41a43a2f6bf88503c6a91ce5518368ecdc85508dd3923c36d5516313397d9cd,bounded_optional,\\\"{'index': 435, 'month': 28, 'stage': 'maintenance_and_capacity_capex', 'cash': '0.01832852059153992475521088993805688', 'shortfall': '0.03167147940846007524478911006194312'}\\\",86.5015371603142717984072734304753101,21.8435774193548387096774193548387097,20.0000000,39.99998340,22812785,0.084136373529141663326069131848654165,False,,,122.900213459495661992916356246524033,-125.313153902837287814141716581244720,0.541113824999999999999999999999999126,7.00831832267405098331268367180092027,30.9001801279113882002477959383889572\\r\\nrescue_bound_optional_equity_price_260.50,d0e67757893f41d2d9ba03a2426512e0cca3293749bd6e739f0ece9eff920004,bounded_optional,\\\"{'index': 435, 'month': 28, 'stage': 'maintenance_and_capacity_capex', 'cash': '0.01832852059153992475521088993805688', 'shortfall': '0.03167147940846007524478911006194312'}\\\",86.5015371603142717984072734304753101,21.8435774193548387096774193548387097,20.0000000,39.99998340,22428908,0.068461112774638872298196595215424665,False,,,125.003684802915092677586994339419456,-125.313153902837287814141716581244720,0.541113824999999999999999999999999126,7.00831832267405098331268367180092027,30.9001801279113882002477959383889572\\r\\n\"","\"# Raksan Transformers Limited | SME research | Master Prompt v3.0\\n\\n## 1. Executive Verdict\\n\\n**Hold — unresolved. BQS 5.2; GQS 5.0 after the cash-quality cap; IAS NS.** Raksan manufactures distribution and power transformers and is investing fresh IPO capital in a larger power/inverter-duty plant. Physical output and operating profitability establish a genuine manufacturing business. However, FY26 manufactured-transformer sales grew only 4.34%, much less than the 12.00% headline revenue increase after new low-margin trading. Three-year reported CFO realizes about 45% of PAT, while receivables, guarantees and investment commitments absorb funding. Recurring bank-return discrepancies, an incompletely reconciled original/restated financial bridge and related-advance terms prevent treating the latest unmodified audit as a clean bill of financial reliability. The ₹260.50 reference price does not cure missing October cash and execution evidence. This is a **manufacturing growth/reinvestment thesis with material quality limitations**, not an evidence-backed compounder or a supported purchase recommendation. A dated bank-supported IPO-to-cash bridge, documented customer collections, plant qualification/commissioning and verified trading evidence could change the conclusion. [Prospectus, printed pp163–213](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n## 2. Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\\n\\n- Exact issuer: **Raksan Transformers Limited**, BSE SME **544924 / RAKSAN**, ISIN **INE1S7M01017**, CIN **U31103DL1995PLC184910**. Incorporated in 1995; public-company conversion in May 2025. Do not confuse it with similarly named entities or Supreme Power Equipment.\\n- Information cutoff: **20 October 2026, Asia/Kolkata**. Sources retrieved 23 October are used only for information available by the cutoff. Reference date: **19 October 2026**, ₹260.50 dated secondary closing-price reference, not a verified executable exchange quote. Five-year horizon ends 19 October 2031.\\n- Current issued shares **20,893,400**, authorized **25,000,000**, ₹10 face value; 400-share market lot. Listing 18 September 2026. The official NSE interoperability record corroborates security/share/lot data, **not an NSE listing or BSE tradeability**. [Share-capital reconciliation](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/reconcilation_share_capital_report.pdf), [dated secondary quote](https://shreni.in/company-profile/raksan-transformers).\\n- Consolidated Indian GAAP, not assumed Ind AS. Restated FY24–FY26 is the principal comparable accounting block; earlier original statements and their qualifications remain separate. Latest comparable FY27 interim/TTM and current cash-flow statement: **ND**, not estimated from PAT.\\n- Nominal equity hurdle **15% before investor taxes**, sensitivity 12%/18%. Separately assumed operating discount rate 15%, sensitivity 12%/18%; numerical coincidence does not make equity hurdle equal WACC by definition. Analytical cash floor ₹0.05 crore, stressed at ₹0.25/1/2 crore. No actual position supplied; liquidity reference **₹5 lakh**, not an allocation recommendation.\\n\\n| Gate | Status | Issue / resolution |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| G1 | Conditional | Recurring historical controls/RPT inconsistencies; no substantiated severe diversion or minority abuse established. Resolve with: Independent loan terms, commercial benchmarking and relevant-party recovery documentation. |\\n| G2 | Hold — unresolved | Material bank-return, restatement-vintage, related-loan and debt-table differences remain unresolved. Resolve with: Issuer/auditor reconciliation supported by bank statements and ledger extracts. |\\n| G3 | Hold — unresolved | March-to-October cash, IPO disbursement and committed drawable facilities not verified; scenarios can breach before IPO. This is not demonstrated actual insolvency. Resolve with: Verified dated cash/debt bridge, covenant/drawing-power and essential capex/WC funding. |\\n| G4 | Hold — unresolved | No complete official postlisting turnover/spread/circuit/restriction evidence. Resolve with: Official tradability, observed daily tape including no-trade sessions and executable lot/spread evidence. |\\n\\nConfidence: **Medium** on historical business, revenue decomposition and capital-return proxies; **Medium** on governance findings, with Low confidence that unresolved items are immaterial; **Low** on current cash/commitments, valuation and tradability. Overall investment confidence is therefore **Low**, not an average. A modeled historical cash breach is evidence that assumptions need validation, not proof that the company actually defaulted.\\n\\n## 3. Scorecard and Calculation Audit\\n\\n| Measure | Raw | Final | Coverage | Gap / cap |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| BQS | 5.18 | 5.2 | 100.00% | No numerical override. |\\n| GQS | 6.50 | 5.0 | 100.00% | Persistent three-year weak cash realization triggers growth-quality cap5. |\\n| IAS | NS | NS | 45.00% | R/P/L unavailable; no weight redistribution. |\\n\\nExact BQS arithmetic: 0.80 GOV + 1.00 MOAT + 0.96 REV + 0.60 DUR + 0.72 CAP + 0.30 CASH + 0.40 BAL + 0.40 EXEC = **5.18**. GQS: 3.20 REV + 1.20 DUR + 0.90 EARN + 0.90 CAP + 0.30 CASH = **6.50**, capped at **5.00** because poor realization persists across three profitable years. This is not a penalty for expansion capex: capex is investing cash flow and cannot explain weak CFO.\\n\\nIAS reuses unrounded final BQS: 0.25×5.18 + 0.20×4 = **2.095 known contribution**; R/P/L missing weight **0.55**; coverage **45%**. Exact mathematical missing-data bound **[2.645, 7.595]**, not a confidence interval, valuation range or rankable score. No midpoint, renormalization or hidden haircut. Neither governance nor funding numerical failure override is applied because an evidenced severe failure is not established. Gate holds nevertheless preclude a favorable investment classification.\\n\\n| Factor | Score | Confidence | Evidence and contrary view |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| GOV | 4 | Medium | Historical audit qualifications and FY22 missing verification documentation are recurrent. SHR related purchases44.70cr plus terms-undefined advance1.42cr and bank-return discrepancies require scrutiny. Contrary: FY26 unmodified audit/effective IFC and later physical verification are improvements; no severe diversion established. [audit_old, rpt, bank_returns, audit_current] |\\n| MOAT | 5 | Medium | BIS/BEE qualification and in-house testing support participation. Two operating plants and repeat government utility customers demonstrate useful execution capability. Contrary: Lowest-bid tenders, weak bargaining and 2019 temporary exclusion prevent a durable-pricing-moat conclusion. [qualification_execution, prospectus] |\\n| REV | 8 | Medium | Scored window FY23–FY26 reported consolidated nominal revenue72.367795→363.1082cr, CAGR71.20%; not organic. Removing new FY26 trading gives endpoint337.7289cr and CAGR67.11%, still≥30% band. Manufactured transformer revenue160.19→322.53→336.52cr; trading separately removed. Physical distribution output822278→1375253KVA and power305.85→1285MVA support real expansion. Contrary: Latest manufactured sales growth4.34%, versus12.00% headline growth; five-year FY21 standalone/COVID series is context only, not the scored basis. Original/restated GAAP and unseparated price/service/mix limit confidence. Starting three-year ≥30% schedule9, limited to8 by Medium-confidence ceiling; no second discretionary haircut. [prospectus, audit2023] |\\n| DUR | 6 | Medium | June2026 confirmed order estimate329.68cr and83orders provides specific demand visibility. New project adds1900MVA power and704MVA inverter-duty capacity, planned December2026. Contrary: Tenders can cancel/defer; 58.56% UP revenue and new capacity qualification/commissioning not yet achieved. [prospectus, capacity] |\\n| CAP | 6 | Medium | FY24–26 observed incremental NOPAT exceeds incremental invested capital cost benchmark. Expanded power mix and utilization show existing assets earning more. Contrary: Prior margin/utilization improvement is not new-project IRR; ₹72.58cr project plus higher working capital means reinvestment returns not yet proven, especially with restatement/capital-payable bridge limits. [prospectus, capacity] |\\n| CASH | 3 | Medium | FY24–26 CFO/PAT ratio of sums≈0.45, not average of annual ratios. Receivables rose20.12→73.21cr and original/recast FCF remains thin/negative cumulatively. Contrary: CFO stayed positive across all three restated years and improvedFY26; growth explains assets, not automatic cash discipline. Poor realization persists across three profitable years, so GQS cap5 applies. [prospectus] |\\n| BAL | 5 | Medium | September fresh IPO gross120.47cr, net modeled108.74cr, substantially increases funding. March debt20.74cr is below one year EBITDA, with no reported default. Contrary: Net proceeds earmarked for capex/WC/debt, almost no March free cash, callable CC, guarantee commitments and June debt-total discrepancy constrain stress resilience. [prospectus, allotment, debt, guarantees] |\\n| EXEC | 5 | Medium | Physical throughput and power-transformer mix increased sharplyFY24–FY25. FY26 plant utilization exceeds90% for both main product classes. Contrary: Delay penalties recur; new plant promised December2026 is not delivered as of cutoff; 2019 qualification exclusion remains part of history. [prospectus, capacity, qualification_execution] |\\n| EARN | 6 | Medium | FY26 restated operating EBITDA growth is largely operating rather than other-income driven. Owners PAT improved20.38→33.60cr despite IPO-equivalent EPS denominator dilution. Contrary: Margin expansion while manufactured growth slows, original-to-restated PAT adjustment and weak cash conversion reduce durability; CFO concern scored separately inCASH. [prospectus, audit2026c] |\\n| R | NS | Low | Complete funded and unfunded counterfactual paths built. Base pre-entry/intraperiod cash can breach before IPO even with positive terminal accounting cash. Contrary: Current October funding/timing not verified; cash-cleared conditional branches are not a defensible unconditional return estimate. [model, debt] |\\n| D | 4 | Medium | Guarantee/receivable/working-capital/capex stresses can produce a cash shortfall. Whole-share rescues consume bounded bank/equity capacity, are not assured. Contrary: Fresh equity and tangible operating capacity provide some cushion; stress breach is not evidence of actual insolvency. [model, guarantees] |\\n| P | NS | Low | Reference market cap and reported multiples are calculated. Earned terminal value requires reinvestment and self-funding, not arbitrary PE. Contrary: Entry cash/commitments unreconciled and conditional terminal results cannot establish a supported valuation cushion. [model, debt] |\\n| L | NS | Low | 400share lot verified; reference cost104200rupees. ListingSeptember18 leaves short trading history. Contrary: Official postlisting turnover, spread, circuit/restriction state not established. Missing observations are ND, prelisting NA. [market, capital_reconciliation] |\\n\\nFactors use the same canonical values across scores. REV starts at 9 on the ≥30% historical growth schedule and is limited to 8 by Medium confidence/relevant-history limits, not reduced twice for the same limitation. CAP and EXEC ±1-point sensitivity produces BQS 4.98–5.38; GQS remains capped at 5 because CASH stays 3. These are judgment sensitivities, not different factual gate conclusions. Full factors, contributions, bounds and nine perturbations are machine-readable.\\n\\n## 4. Business Overview\\n\\nRaksan earns manufacturing revenue from distribution and power transformers, plus repair/service/other activity and FY26 trading. FY26 product revenue includes distribution ₹233.0351 crore, power ₹100.1422 crore and other ₹29.9309 crore. Distribution transformers connect local distribution networks; higher-capacity power transformers address utility/industrial projects. Manufacturing requires conductive metals, electrical steel, insulation, testing and customer acceptance; revenue is not pure engineering value added.\\n\\nGovernment customers represented **50.73%** of FY26 sales versus **72.99%** in FY25. Uttar Pradesh contributed **58.56%**; six states together **97.13%**. A lower government percentage does not demonstrate broad geographic diversification. Tender awards, manufacturing, inspection/dispatch, billing, collection and release of guarantees/retention are different milestones. Accounting sales can therefore grow before discretionary cash. [Prospectus, business/customer/geography disclosures, printed pp112–129](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nThe consolidated Haryana Power Industries **partnership** was controlled from November 2015; ownership increased from 95% to 99.99% on 19 May 2025 for ₹0.0437 crore minority consideration. FY26 external revenue was nil and loss ₹0.1592 crore. That ownership change is not the source of headline manufacturing growth. A separate same-name HUF/proprietary related counterparty must not be conflated with the consolidated entity. [Prospectus, group and related-party notes](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n## 5. Moat / Industry Position\\n\\n**Useful qualification and execution capability, not demonstrated durable pricing power.** ISO processes, BIS eligibility up to the disclosed distribution ratings, BEE efficiency ratings and internal testing facilitate approved-vendor participation. They do not eliminate competing qualified suppliers, lowest-price bidding, raw-material exposure, inspection failure or customer concentration. The issuer disclosed exclusion from three consecutive PVVNL tenders under a 20 June 2019 order. The business continued afterward, but the history demonstrates that eligibility is not permanent. [Prospectus, printed pp22,124](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nNo contract-level evidence establishes universal or timely copper/electrical-steel price pass-through. Price-escalation clauses can protect the ultimate invoice while still leaving a timing gap, excluded items, benchmark mismatch or tender-margin compression. Inventory and funding requirements remain even where eventual pass-through exists. The January 2026 rating supports business continuity but its liquidity forecast is not a bank commitment. [Infomerics, 13 January 2026](https://infomericstorage.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/pr_raksan_transformers_13jan26_8d9de3f012.pdf), [10 February 2025](https://www.infomerics.com/admin/uploads/pr-raksan-transformers-10feb25.pdf).\\n\\nEconomic comparators:\\n\\n- **Shilchar Technologies** is the stronger historical margin/export-diversification reference: FY25 revenue about ₹623 crore, approximately 30% EBITDA margin, 43% exports and stated net cash ₹91 crore. These are FY25 historical facts, not current comparable valuation inputs. They show that technology/product/customer mix and cash generation matter beyond generic transformer demand. [FY25 report, printed pp2–4,14–15](https://shilchar.com/upload/power_investor_relations/annual-report-2024-2025.pdf).\\n- **Supreme Power Equipment** offers a commissioning/qualification comparison. Its June 2026 release says February commissioning increased capacity from 2,500 to 9,000 MVA with capability up to 200 MVA/220kV. Those **9,000 MVA belong to Supreme, not Raksan**. Management's ₹500–550 crore full-utilization sales potential is not an independently verified revenue guarantee. Conflicting income/PAT labels in that release are not imported into a profitability ranking. [Exchange release, pp2–3](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/SPEL_01062026185238_SPELH2FY26PressRelease.pdf).\\n- **Marsons** is an issuer-selected peer with lower FY26 closing-equity RONW than Shilchar in the prospectus comparison. That one ratio does not establish lower total business quality. Its old annual-report link returned 404; a fresh independently reconciled audit comparison remains incomplete.\\n\\nThe prospectus peer P/Es, 49.63x Marsons, 29.47x Shilchar and 27.75x Supreme, use **28 August 2026** prices and their own share/earnings bases. They are neither current comparable quotes nor permission to apply a 30x exit multiple to Raksan. [Prospectus, printed p96](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n## 6. Revenue Growth & Scale\\n\\nOriginal audited history, retained without splicing into the restated cash/capital series:\\n\\n| FY | Scope | Revenue | Owners PAT | CFO | Cash capex |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2020 | Standalone, FY21 comparative; pre-restatement | 61.61 | 1.76 | ND | ND |\\n| 2021 | Standalone original, qualified | 34.22 | 0.07 | 1.43 | 4.01 |\\n| 2022 | Consolidated original FY23 comparative, uncorrected AS15/MSME | 58.26 | 0.74 | -1.07 | 0.04 |\\n| 2023 | Consolidated original, subject-to AS15/MSME | 72.37 | 3.47 | 5.59 | 0.33 |\\n\\nFY20 is an earlier comparison year, not a seventh fully reconstructed annual cash-flow record. FY21 is a COVID trough and standalone; FY22–23 consolidated comparatives carry old audit/control limitations. Headline historical CAGR: **3y 2023–2026: 71.20% (₹72.37→363.11 crore); 5y 2021–2026: 60.38% (₹34.22→363.11 crore)**. A reliable ten-year CAGR is ND. These are nominal revenue CAGRs, not organic volume or intrinsic-value growth. **The scored REV window is FY23–FY26 reported consolidated revenue, ₹72.367795→₹363.1082 crore, approximately71.20% CAGR.** The same controlled-subsidiary perimeter is used, but the old original/restated GAAP qualifications limit confidence. The FY21 standalone/COVID trough makes the five-year series context only, not the primary scoring basis. As a robustness check, removing new FY26 trading gives endpoint₹337.7289 crore and approximately67.11% nominal CAGR, still within the same ≥30% starting band. This check is not a complete constant-price manufactured-sales CAGR: earlier service, price and mix are not fully separable. The FY24–FY26 physical-output evidence below supports genuine manufacturing expansion, without relabeling all nominal growth organic.\\n\\n| FY | Revenue addition | YoY |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 2021 | -27.39 | -44.46% |\\n| 2022 | 24.04 | 70.25% |\\n| 2023 | 14.11 | 24.22% |\\n| 2024 | 88.58 | 122.40% |\\n| 2025 | 163.26 | 101.44% |\\n| 2026 | 38.90 | 12.00% |\\n\\nThe manufactured-sales bridge is more informative: FY24 **₹160.1914 crore**, FY25 **₹322.5265 crore**, FY26 **₹336.5174 crore**. FY26 trading sales **₹25.3793 crore** on purchases **₹25.2732 crore** imply only **₹0.1061 crore** gross spread before other costs. Manufacturing increased ₹13.9909 crore, **4.34%**, while headline revenue increased ₹38.8984 crore, approximately **12.00%**. Trading alone contributes ₹25.3793 crore; the residual other-sales mix declines about ₹0.4718 crore. It is wrong to call all headline growth organic manufacturing expansion. [Prospectus, revenue and purchases notes, printed pp193–196](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nPhysical output corroborates real prior growth: distribution **822,278 → 1,175,472 → 1,375,253 KVA** and power **305.85 → 1,156.75 → 1,285 MVA** in FY24–FY26. FY26 growth includes mix and pricing, but contract-level price/volume decomposition is ND. Distribution output grew about17% and power about11%, while aggregate manufactured value grew4.34%; changing mix/realizations therefore matter. No independently measured market-share gain is asserted. [Prospectus, capacity/production tables](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n## 7. Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\\n\\nAt 30 June 2026 the issuer reported **83 confirmed orders, estimated unexecuted value ₹329.6792 crore**. The figure is not guaranteed near-term sales or cash: escalation, freight/taxes, delivery changes, cancellation, inspections and collections affect conversion. No customer-level cash-secured backlog reconciliation was located. Larger utility investment is an accessible demand opportunity, not proof Raksan wins a fixed market share. [Prospectus, order-book disclosures](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nExisting annual capacity is **1,500 MVA distribution + 1,350 MVA power = 2,850 MVA**; FY26 utilization91.68%/95.18%. The new project adds **1,900 MVA power +704 MVA inverter duty**, yielding **5,454 MVA** combined capacity, not9,000. Distribution capacity does not increase. Target commissioning and Consent to Operate: **December2026**, a management milestone not delivered as of cutoff. Capacity does not equal customer-approved saleable output. [Capacity certificate](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/proposed_capacity_post_expansion.pdf), [Prospectus, objects/business](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nProject budget **₹72.5843 crore**, already-paid **₹10.4477 crore**, IPO-funded remainder **₹62.1366 crore**. The engineer certificate shows₹72.5837 crore, a ₹0.0006 crore rounding/estimate difference retained rather than hidden. Land is not included in this incremental project budget. Incremental sales capacity near₹600 crore is an analytical mix/price approximation, not issuer guidance: FY26 power revenue/MVA is about₹0.0779 crore, and distribution differs materially. Beyond₹600 crore sales the model charges₹0.35 of additional fixed-capital investment per incremental revenue rupee, plus working capital and restricted deposits. The ratio roughly links project cost per new MVA to FY26 power realizations; new product mix, qualification and execution can invalidate it.\\n\\nGQS6.50 raw does not mean growth is already self-funded. GQS is capped5.00 by persistent CASH3. Existing margin/utilization improvement can lift observed incremental ROIC without proving attractive returns on the proposed plant. Cash collection and capital efficiency, not a growing order headline alone, must earn an improved score.\\n\\n## 8. Management, Governance & Execution\\n\\nThe original audit record was inspected across FY21/FY22 standalone, FY23–FY26 consolidated and FY26 standalone, including annexures and notes, rather than relying only on the IPO summary.\\n\\n- **FY21** explicitly qualified unaccounted AS15 gratuity and MSMED supplier interest. Similar issues recur through subsequent early reports. **FY22 CARO** says PPE records/physical-verification and inventory-verification documentation were not produced. FY22 March bank debtors were₹12.277766 crore versus books₹15.267245 crore, difference₹2.989479 crore; stock book comparison was not available. [FY21 audit p1](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2021.pdf), [FY22 annexures pp7–8,16](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2022.pdf).\\n- **FY26** original opinion is unmodified, IFC described effective and audit-trail operation/preservation reported. Later PPE/inventory verification is a real improvement, not erasure of historical limitations. The original FY25 first-page opinion appears unmodified while the prospectus describes FY24/FY25 modified reports; the wording conflict remains unresolved. [FY26 standalone audit](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf), [prospectus pp163–164](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n- **Recurring bank-return differences remain material.** FY26 Q4 book/bank inventory₹25.9117/20.2383 crore; receivables₹73.2119/60.4163; payables₹43.5185/37.2298. Differences₹5.6734/12.7956/6.2887 crore. Explanations mention unclosed quarters, year-end adjustments, excluded WIP and net advances. They are not transaction-level reconciliations or evidence of unrestricted cash. [FY26 standalone Annexure C](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf), [prospectus pp178–179](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n- Related-party **SHR Powers** purchases₹44.7038 crore, sales₹2.2731 crore and closing advance₹1.4209 crore are significant. FY26 Annexure D describes an advance in the nature of a loan with undefined terms; CAROiii(c–e) cannot comment on repayment/overdues, whileiii(f) is inconsistent about unspecified-term related advances. Demand signed terms, purpose, arm's-length benchmarking and recovery, not a presumption of theft. Sanjeev remuneration₹1.50 crore plus₹0.0125 crore bonus/leave, Dievam salary₹0.48 crore and related rent₹0.468 crore are disclosed. [Prospectus pp56–58,199,204](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf), [standalone Annexure D](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf).\\n- A proposed related-property sale carries₹0.31 crore advance and December2027 deadline. Price-unit wording is ambiguous; no future sale cash is assumed. Missing old ROC forms, minutes and transfer deeds plus filing errors are disclosed. No material criminal litigation or proven severe minority abuse is established by the reviewed evidence. [Prospectus pp28–29 and related-party notes](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n| Dated commitment / result | Evidence as of cutoff | Interpretation |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| FY24–FY26 throughput expansion | Power output305.85→1,285MVA | Demonstrated execution, not merely announced capacity |\\n| FY25/FY26 deliveries | Late-delivery charges₹3.2017/2.6384crore | Recurring cost, not penalty-free execution |\\n| December2026 new-plant target | Not yet commissioned by20October | Remains forecast; test0/6/12-month delay |\\n| FY26 AGM timing | Extension to5December2026 | Track completion; extension itself is not fraud |\\n\\n[Late-delivery/warranty notes and project schedule](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf), [AGM extension](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/agm_extention_intimation.pdf).\\n\\n## 9. Financial Forensics\\n\\nRestated consolidated history, ₹crore, Indian GAAP. Operating EBIT = PBT + finance cost − other income; operating EBITDA adds D&A. This removes non-operating income, not every possible normalization. No undisclosed margin uplift is added. PAT and CFO use matching consolidated scope; owners PAT drives EPS.\\n\\n| FY | Revenue | Operating EBITDA | Owners PAT | CFO | Cash capex | FCF | Debt | Free cash | IC proxy |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2024 | 160.95 | 10.93 | 7.59 | 7.43 | 2.49 | 4.94 | 9.81 | 4.64 | 29.76 |\\n| 2025 | 324.21 | 29.78 | 20.38 | 5.36 | 27.63 | -22.27 | 23.51 | 0.21 | 68.72 |\\n| 2026 | 363.11 | 47.10 | 33.60 | 14.89 | 11.30 | 3.58 | 20.74 | 0.23 | 103.10 |\\n\\nThree-year CFO/PAT 44.95%; cash-interest-adjusted 41.59%; reported FCF sum ₹-13.75 crore; after capital advances ₹-15.99 crore; two-year incremental ROIC 35.97%.\\n\\nThe cash issue is receivables and operating reinvestment, not merely capex. Receivables rose₹20.1219→52.0221→73.2119crore; inventory₹19.4491→21.2447→25.9117; payables₹26.6862→42.4227→43.5185. FY26's₹21.1898crore AR increase exceeds CFO₹14.8853crore. Average AR/total-revenue days is a labeled proxy for credit-revenue days. Comparable gross-profit, credit-purchases and asset-level maintenance splits areND where not unambiguously separated; no synthetic gross margin is substituted for disclosed operating EBITDA. Contract assets/retention are not independently disclosed enough to assert a clean cash-conversion cycle; inventory/payable days with compatible purchasing denominators remain ND rather than mixing misleading denominators.\\n\\n| FY | NOPAT at25% tax | IC | ROIC average | 1y incremental ROIC | Average AR days proxy |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2024 | 7.91 | 29.76 | ND | ND | ND |\\n| 2025 | 21.62 | 68.72 | 43.90% | 35.18% | 40.61 |\\n| 2026 | 34.29 | 103.10 | 39.92% | 36.88% | 62.94 |\\n\\nIC funding-side bridge adds equity, NCI, funded debt, capital creditors, tax/financing/property-advance exclusions from operating liabilities, and subtracts available cash, DTA and non-operating investments. Restricted/security deposits remain operating invested capital, not debt-netting cash. FY26 direct asset-side IC: ONWC49.3075 + fixed/CWIP45.2435 + capital advances2.2439 + deposits6.3066 =₹103.1015crore, versus funding-side₹103.1013; ₹0.0002 rounding difference. FY24 payables components sum₹2,668.63 lakh versus printed₹2,668.62; this table uses the printed total. FY25 components sum₹4,242.27 lakh versus printed₹4,242.28; this table retains the component sum. Each ₹0.01 lakh difference is ₹0.0001 crore, explicitly retained rather than treated as a substantive reconciliation. Reconciled residual ONWC is also retained. NOPAT uses an explicit25% normalized operating tax assumption; actual taxes differ. Average-capital ROIC/ROCE differs from issuer closing-equity RONW. Three/five-year comparable incremental ROIC is **ND** because earlier capital classifications/qualifications are not reconciled, not because older evidence was ignored. Two-year incremental proxy is not marginal project IRR; utilization, product mix and margin improvement can dominate it. [Prospectus, statements/notes pp166–209](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nOriginal-vintage conflicts are explicit. FY26 original PAT₹33.3531→restated33.6048crore is bridged by removing₹0.2539prior-year tax and₹0.0022additional depreciation. CFO14.8871→14.8853, equity77.5941→77.4159; original investment property0.7883 disappears and PPE39.8193→40.5695. Reclassification net of accumulated depreciation is consistent with part of that movement but is not a complete issuer-certified balance bridge. FY25 original comparative PAT20.7637→20.3767 differs₹0.3870. Do not combine original equity with restated profits. FY23 reported cash₹8.323753 included₹7.267057restricted margin deposits: genuinely available cash₹1.056696. [FY26 original consolidated statements](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_consolidated_signed_2025_26.pdf), [FY23 consolidated](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2023.pdf).\\n\\n**IPO and debt bridge.** Pre-IPO16,480,600 shares + fresh4,412,800 =20,893,400; OFS1,100,000 transfers old holdings and supplies no corporate cash. At₹273, fresh gross₹120.46944crore less modeled issuer expenses₹11.7302 =₹108.73924net. Objects: capex62.1366, WC35, debt7.2834, GCP4.3192crore; ₹0.00004difference is rounding. Fresh issuance dilutes old proportional ownership by21.12%; 18:1 bonus is not economic dilution. Post-issue book before subsequent operating movements should add **net**, not gross proceeds:₹186.15514crore. Issuer gross-proceeds NAV is not net usable cash. The prospectus expressly reports no outstanding convertible instruments, warrants or conversion rights and no promoter/group pledge at its date. The30September shareholding reports promoter/group15,380,600shares (73.61%), including Sanjeev13,003,662 (62.24%); public26.39% is not equivalent to actively tradable free float after lock-ins. Future equity is explicit uncommitted scenario funding, not a disclosed planned issue. [30September shareholding](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/shareholding_pattern_bse_30.9.26.pdf). [Allotment](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/basis_of_allotment_advertisement.pdf), [prospectus capital/objects](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nMarch debt₹20.7364crore, free cash₹0.2257crore. June funded debt rows sum **₹29.7773crore**, not printed₹26.1274; ₹3.6499difference nearly equals the new May₹3.65LAP. March debt plus CC increase₹5.7219 and May draw equals₹30.1083. Model June principal₹0.3310reconciles the row sum, explicitly an **assumption**, not verified cash flow. Later principal₹0.18/month is separately stressed. Old LAP₹7.3648 differs from objects table₹7.4134. ₹22.5crore CC sanction, one-year/callable renewal and rating facilities are not verified October undrawn commitments. The model does not automatically roll the facility. [Prospectus pp90,211–213](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nGuarantees₹17.4788crore versus₹4.1673FY25 and capital commitments₹46.7575crore matter beyond reported funded debt. Deposits₹6.3066cannot be spent freely. FY26 warranty settlements₹0.9058crore, closing provision₹0.4744crore; no unsupported claim that provision covers every future warranty. Retention, guarantee-release and procurement-price protection schedules are ND. Rent remains an operating cost; no unverified lease capitalization or property-sale proceeds are fabricated.\\n\\n## 10. Valuation & Market Expectations\\n\\nReference calculations, not current enterprise value: **market_cap=544.27; pe_postipo_equivalent=16.20; ev_march_debt_cash_reference=564.78; ev_ebitda_march_reference=11.99; postipo_equivalent_eps=16.08; book_march=77.42; proforma_book_after_net_fresh_issue=186.16; pb_net_proceeds_proforma=2.92**. Post-IPO equivalent EPS uses current issued shares against FY26 owners earnings, not the smaller historical IPO EPS denominator. Current October EV is **ND** until cash/debt/use-of-proceeds reconciles. Apparently modest historical P/E is not automatically cheap after new capex, cash retention, minority/control risk and execution limitations.\\n\\nThe linked model begins at audited31March2026, with seven dated pre-entry buckets through19October, then60monthly post-entry buckets and12monthly terminal-continuation buckets. Each bucket exposes customer receipts, cash costs, WC, restricted deposits, taxes, interest, capex, repayments and remaining receipts. Revenues are annual trajectories, not a quarterly annualization. Project attribution of March CWIP/advances, cash spent by entry₹25crore and IPO cash date30September are assumptions with sensitivity. Original capital-payable settlement is separated from new project assets. Opening fixed₹41.5881crore plus project₹5.8993crore totals₹47.4874: capital advances₹2.2439 are outside the₹45.2435fixed/CWIP figure and included once, not deducted twice. Intangible development₹0.0793 remains inside the modeled fixed approximation; the3.5%depreciation is an explicit estimate, not a purported asset-level issuer schedule. All initial balances, code and formulas are included.\\n\\nAssumptions (not guidance): bear sales₹370/380/410/450/490crore and margins7.5/7.5/8/8.5/8.5%; base₹450/525/610/690/760 and12/12/11.5/11/11%; bull₹520/650/800/950/1,100 and13.5/13/12.5/12/12%. Pre-entry annual sales360/400/430 and margins9/12/13%. Before commissioning, post-entry annualized revenue is capped₹400crore without later catch-up. Bear capex25%overrun and12-month delay. AR110/80/70days; inventory11/9/8%revenue, payables8/10.5/11%; cash operating costs paid before the last10%of receipts. This ordering is a stress convention, not a verified monthly settlement sequence.\\n\\n| Case | First cash breach | Entry cash / debt | Terminal cash / debt | Conditional return | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| bear_none | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹8.21 | 26.27 / 21.84 | -8.06 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bear_bounded_optional | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹8.21 | 26.27 / 21.84 | -8.06 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| base_none | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹1.71 | 70.77 / 21.84 | 100.15 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| base_bounded_optional | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹1.71 | 70.77 / 21.84 | 100.15 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bull_none | m-7 cash_taxes; shortfall₹0.84 | 86.50 / 21.84 | 64.03 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bull_bounded_optional | m-7 cash_taxes; shortfall₹0.84 | 86.50 / 21.84 | 64.03 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n\\n**Every ordinary bear/base/bull path breaches before IPO under its timing assumptions. No ordinary IRR is reported.** Later positive cash is a counterfactual rollforward, not survival. Post-entry optional funding is prohibited from curing that earlier failure. Higher cash-floor stress can fail at the audited opening itself; that result is retained, not silently recentered to a cash-rich IPO date.\\n\\nOptional rescue, only before a new post-entry breach: maximum₹20crore gross bank draw at12%, immediate draw-month interest,12-month grace then36-month repayment; maximum₹40crore gross equity at₹208.40,3%fees, **integer whole shares**, bounded by25million authorized capital and4,106,600new-share ceiling. Draw/issuance totals remain bounded even after prior debt amortizes. This is not committed finance. Existing debt runs off without automatic CC renewal. Optional branches never receive ordinary IRR.\\n\\nFor diagnosis only, a separate conditional branch assumes all pre-entry monthly receipts arrive before costs, AR70days and bull pre-entry activity. This optimistic cash-clear bridge is **not observed October cash**. It reveals which post-entry economics survive instead of falsely rehabilitating the main failed paths:\\n\\n| AR days / margin / funding | Bank / equity gross | Dilution | Survival | Conditional IRR | Counterfactual terminal price |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 80_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 144.97 |\\n| 80_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 129.22 |\\n| 80_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 219.89 |\\n| 80_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 197.06 |\\n| 80_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | True | 3.05% | 302.68 |\\n| 80_.12_bounded_optional | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | True | 3.05% | 302.68 |\\n| 100_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 134.45 |\\n| 100_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 122.90 |\\n| 100_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 209.36 |\\n| 100_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 191.07 |\\n| 100_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 284.28 |\\n| 100_.12_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 257.27 |\\n| 120_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 123.92 |\\n| 120_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 113.50 |\\n| 120_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 198.84 |\\n| 120_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 182.11 |\\n| 120_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 273.75 |\\n| 120_.12_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 250.65 |\\n\\nEarned terminal EV is next-year FCFF/(WACC−g), not an arbitrary exit P/E. FCFF deducts25%operating tax, maintenance at1.25×modeled D&A, fixed-capital growth, working-capital/restricted-deposit growth, **and growth of required operating liquidity**. D&A is3.5%of operating fixed capital; maintenance1.0/1.25/1.5× and debt rates10/11.45/14%are tested. Required operating cash reserve is solved over every unlevered continuation prefix with a growing reserve; g×reserve is segregated and deducted from FCFF. A distinct cash continuation pays all remaining debt and declining interest. Debt is deducted **once** from EV plus cash above the operating reserve, not also hidden inside the valuation reserve. No dividends or property-sale windfalls assumed.\\n\\nSelected branch: conditional_preentry_clear_stress_80_.12_none. Survives modeled cash tests, not observed entry funding.\\n\\n| WACC / perpetual growth | 2% | 4% | 6% |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 12.00% | 382.66 | 413.23 | 464.17 |\\n| 15.00% | 296.29 | 302.68 | 311.90 |\\n| 18.00% | 242.31 | 239.51 | 235.77 |\\n\\nConditional entry prices for that selected branch, not a supported unconditional fair-value range:\\n\\n| Hurdle | Conditional entry price | After2% entry and2% exit friction |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 12.00% | 171.75 | 165.01 |\\n| 15.00% | 150.48 | 144.58 |\\n| 18.00% | 132.30 | 127.12 |\\n\\nThe2%entry/2%exit friction example is an assumption, not measured spreads or an execution promise. Discount/growth matrix, margin/growth grid, AR60/80/100/120days, front receipts85/90/95/100%, terminal timing80/90/100%, capex/delay, retention0/2.5/5%ofsales, CCrunoff1/13/25months, IPOdelay, principal bridge, guarantees0/10/100%, openingproject attribution and rescue-price/cap sensitivities are retained. No rerating multiple is needed to earn value; weak FCFF or inability to continue suppresses return scoreability.\\n\\nReverse expectations use the cash-clear conditional history, starting revenue₹400crore, revenue CAGR−20%to100%grid, then24bisections only across adjacent surviving sign changes. A failed intermediate candidate invalidates that bracket, rather than being assigned a return. **All candidate paths, including failures, are retained.**\\n\\n| Funding | Hurdle | Candidates | Roots | Scope |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| none | 12.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 15.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 18.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 37.97% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 58.49% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 12.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 15.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 18.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 37.97% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 58.49% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n\\nNo bracketed root means none found in the stated surviving domain, not impossibility for all conceivable financing or assumptions. The unconstrained algebraic root of a failed cash path is not an investable expectation.\\n\\nLiquidity: a400-share lot costs₹104,200; four lots₹416,800, five₹521,000beforefees. For the₹5lakhreference, actual sizing is discrete. Official20/60-session turnover means/medians, postlisting zero-trade counts, spread and current restrictions areND; dates before18September areNA, not zero volume. The dated secondary19October volume60,800is a one-day cross-check only. Liquidation days at2/5/10%participation remainND without the prescribed conservative mean/median daily value. L and G4 cannot be cleared from one active day or the existence of an interoperability record.\\n\\n## 11. Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\\n\\n**High impairment risk under linked stress, with uncertain actual funding resilience.** Tender deferral/lost qualification reduces throughput; fixed costs and raw-material mismatch depress margins; slower collections and retention increase funded WC; project overrun consumes earmarked IPO cash; a callable CC renewal or guarantee call then arrives before collection. Lenders and suppliers have prior claims; existing shareholders face dilution, forced asset realization or impaired future earning power. A temporary quoted drawdown is different from this funding/earning-capacity impairment.\\n\\nBear adds₹1.74788crore guarantee cash call (10%ofMarchguarantees),₹3.660595ARnoncollection (5%ofMarchAR),₹1.4209relatedadvance loss and25%projectoverrun. Full-guarantee sensitivity is also retained. These are linked analytical losses, not assertions of existing fraud/default. The exact ordinary bear price loss is **NS** because its cash bridge fails; printing a normal target-price return would conceal the financing problem. Conditional terminal-price diagnostics are not claim-recovery estimates.\\n\\nThe most important thesis-break variable is **verified customer cash collection sufficient to fund essential WC and commissioning without unfavorable rescue**. Strongest opposing evidence to this cautious view: a profitable real manufacturer, high utilization, improving reported CFO, fresh equity and an unmodifiedFY26audit. None independently resolves the dated liquidity/control evidence gaps. A documented serious minority-abuse finding would change G1 to evidenced failure; ordinary volatility alone would not.\\n\\n## 12. 5× / 10× Feasibility\\n\\nFivefold price growth over five years requires about37.97%annualized; tenfold58.49%. Per-share outcomes depend on revenue×margin×valuation **divided by diluted shares**, not merely enterprise sales. The reverse tests above include both multiples, with every cash/funding path retained. Optional equity can raise enterprise survival probability while reducing existing-holder value. A lower terminal capitalization is covered by18%discount/2%growth, not by pretending a high peer P/E persists.\\n\\nThe commissioned capacity/mix approximation is near₹600crore annual sales; larger revenues require new fixed investment, WC, qualification, customers and cash collection. No verified market-share bridge supports several multiples of that capacity or repeated capital raising on favorable terms. **5×/10× are speculative / unsupported as current investment theses**, even if a conditional numerical root appears in an optimistic financing domain. There is no defensible success probability or price target.\\n\\n## 13. Monitoring Plan\\n\\nResearch checkpoints only; no automatic trade or reminder is created.\\n\\n| KPI / event | Baseline | Warning / investigation | Thesis-break / clearance evidence | Review source / timing |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Cash and IPO use | Marchfreecash0.2257; netfresh108.73924 | Disbursement cannot reconcile to banks | Essential payments unsupported without rescue; clear only with dated bank/ledger bridge | First post-IPO results/use-of-proceeds report |\\n| Manufactured growth | FY26growth4.34% | Headline growth again led by thin-spread trading | Manufacturing stagnation alongside financed expansion | Each comparable half/full year |\\n| Collection | AR73.2119; CFO/PAT3y≈45% | AR growth again exceeds manufacturing sales/cash growth | Material noncollection or unexplained receivable ageing | Audited ageing/collections; at least half-yearly |\\n| Bank reconciliations | MarchARdifference12.7956 | New material unreconciled returns | Evidence of deliberate material misstatement, or verified remediation to clear G2 | Auditor/issuer Annexure C and bank evidence |\\n| Plant | Dec2026 target; added2604MVA | No permits/testing/customer qualification at target | Costs rise without viable financed commissioning | Completion certificate/Consent to Operate/customer approval |\\n| Capital returns | ICproxy103.1013 | Margin gains do not translate into cash after full capital | Persistently sub-hurdle normalized incremental economics | Full-year cohort and capital bridge |\\n| Guarantees/warranty | Guarantees17.4788; settlement0.9058 | Calls/LDs materially exceed historic pattern | Calls cannot be funded or qualification lost | Utility/issuer disclosures and audited notes |\\n| Related advance | SHR1.4209; undefined terms | No signed repayment/commercial explanation | Evidenced abuse or unrecoverable material related exposure | RPT approvals, loan documents, collections |\\n| Debt | June row-sum29.7773; CCcallable | Renewal/covenants/drawing power unavailable | Verified default or unfinanceable essential obligations | Bank/rating/issuer filings |\\n| Tradability | 400sharelot; short history | One-sided circuits, sparse tape, restrictions | Effectively no executable reference-position exit | Official trading/restriction data before any implementation |\\n\\nThresholds require investigation and causal evidence, not an automatic buy/sell response to a single number.\\n\\n## 14. Final Classification & Conditional Action\\n\\n**Hold — unresolved; research priority only.** Historical quality is mixed (BQS5.18), growth quality limited by cash realization (finalGQS5.00), and IAS isNS. Put this record in **Pending evidence for all batch lists** until critical gate evidence is resolved; do not force it into an ordinal rank or portray it as proven governance failure. It fails compounder requirements independently on quality, cash, moat, governance and unresolved gates.\\n\\nA lower quote alone cannot resolve G2/G3/G4. A better investment assessment requires the missing dated funding/control evidence first, then supported operating assumptions, a fully surviving ordinary return model and implementable liquidity. Conditional prices in section10 are research diagnostics, not instructions. Existing-holder suitability, portfolio concentration, taxes and a specific reduction/exit count are not assessed because no holding information was supplied.\\n\\n## 15. Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\\n\\nEvidence types: **V** primary historical disclosures; **C** exact calculations from identified inputs; **M** management plans/order estimates; **A** analyst forecasts, timing, recovery/funding and valuation assumptions. Primary historical tables areV; score arithmetic, ratios and bridges areC; December commissioning/order realization areM; all post-March operational cash paths and terminal values areA/C. Confidence is attached by subject and canonical factor, not implied by a long source list.\\n\\n| ID | Document / link | Cutoff / scope |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| prospectus | [Prospectus](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2021 | [Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2021](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2021.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2022 | [Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2022](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2022.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2023 | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2023](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2023.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2024c | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2024](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2024.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2025c | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2025](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2025.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2026c | [Consolidated Financial Statements 2025-26](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_consolidated_signed_2025_26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2026s | [Standalone Financial Statements 2025-26](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| capacity | [Proposed Capacity Post Expansion](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/proposed_capacity_post_expansion.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| shareholding | [Shareholding Pattern BSE 30.09.2026](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/shareholding_pattern_bse_30.9.26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| capital_reconciliation | [Reconcilation Share Capital Report](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/reconcilation_share_capital_report.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| allotment | [Basis of Allotment Advertisement](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/basis_of_allotment_advertisement.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| agm | [AGM Extention Intimation](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/agm_extention_intimation.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| rating2026 | [Infomerics January13 2026 credit rationale](https://infomericstorage.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/pr_raksan_transformers_13jan26_8d9de3f012.pdf) | StandaloneBBB/Positive,A3+; source opinion, not bank commitment. |\\n| rating2025 | [Infomerics February10 2025 credit rationale](https://www.infomerics.com/admin/uploads/pr-raksan-transformers-10feb25.pdf) | Earlier orderbook and standalone trajectory; not spliced with restated consolidated financials. |\\n| market_secondary | [Shreni datedOctober19 Raksan market reference](https://shreni.in/company-profile/raksan-transformers) | Price260.50, not execution or official liquidity certification. |\\n| peer_shilchar_2025 | [Shilchar FY25 annual report](https://shilchar.com/upload/power_investor_relations/annual-report-2024-2025.pdf) | Historical FY25 operating comparison, not latest trading or valuation. |\\n| peer_supreme_2026 | [Supreme June1 2026 results and operational release](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/SPEL_01062026185238_SPELH2FY26PressRelease.pdf) | Management commissioning/capacity and qualification comparison; conflicting income/PAT labels not used in valuation. |\\n| nse_interop_20261019 | [NSE October19 2026 interoperability security master](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/cm/interop/NSE_CM_security_19102026.csv.gz) | Two RAKSAN$ rows match ISIN,400sharelot and20,893,400issued shares. No BSE trading/price/circuit conclusion from metadata. |\\n\\nSource locations and transcribed contradictions are retained in the audit ledger; exact original/restated vintages in historical inputs. Issuer statements are generally₹lakh converted by100 to₹crore, with visible rounding differences. Full PDF/OCR binaries are intentionally not redistributed. This package is standalone for reconstructing every research result, not a substitute for reading the linked originals. Peer statements are comparative context, not independently completed peer scoring.\\n\\nMaterial unanswered questions: customer-specific pass-through/retention and collection schedules; actual IPO cash dates/spending; current unrestricted cash and drawable credit; bank-return ledger reconciliation; original-to-restated balance bridge; related-advance terms/recovery; plant permit/qualification milestones; outstanding guarantee release timing; official trade tape and restrictions. These gaps have explicit score/gate consequences, not invented neutral values.\\n\\nReproducibility: **164 unique complete parameter paths; 143 named tests; 250 reverse evaluations, including every failed candidate.** Content-hashed parameter paths and terminal-continuation references preserve all rows losslessly. `canonical.json` is the computational record; `scenario_summary.csv` is a view, not an alternative model. Decimal arithmetic retains unrounded calculations; displayed scores use half-up one-decimal rounding. The external-baseline recovery workflow authenticates every authored input/code file, deletes all generated outputs and attestations, and reconstructs identical outputs without PDFs, network, helpers or private identities. Internal numerical validation is not issuer verification.\\n\\nUpdate record,23October2026: first complete v3 research for the20Octobercutoff; original/restated conflicts, June-debt summation and growing terminal liquidity costs incorporated. No prior v2.2 score is silently compared. No postcutoff operational event or later price is used. Research is conditional and informational, not a financial transaction or personalized allocation recommendation.\\n\"","\"number\"","\"content_markdown\"","\"Executive Verdict\"","\"\\n**Hold — unresolved. BQS 5.2; GQS 5.0 after the cash-quality cap; IAS NS.** Raksan manufactures distribution and power transformers and is investing fresh IPO capital in a larger power/inverter-duty plant. Physical output and operating profitability establish a genuine manufacturing business. However, FY26 manufactured-transformer sales grew only 4.34%, much less than the 12.00% headline revenue increase after new low-margin trading. Three-year reported CFO realizes about 45% of PAT, while receivables, guarantees and investment commitments absorb funding. Recurring bank-return discrepancies, an incompletely reconciled original/restated financial bridge and related-advance terms prevent treating the latest unmodified audit as a clean bill of financial reliability. The ₹260.50 reference price does not cure missing October cash and execution evidence. This is a **manufacturing growth/reinvestment thesis with material quality limitations**, not an evidence-backed compounder or a supported purchase recommendation. A dated bank-supported IPO-to-cash bridge, documented customer collections, plant qualification/commissioning and verified trading evidence could change the conclusion. [Prospectus, printed pp163–213](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n\"","\"Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\"","\"\\n- Exact issuer: **Raksan Transformers Limited**, BSE SME **544924 / RAKSAN**, ISIN **INE1S7M01017**, CIN **U31103DL1995PLC184910**. Incorporated in 1995; public-company conversion in May 2025. Do not confuse it with similarly named entities or Supreme Power Equipment.\\n- Information cutoff: **20 October 2026, Asia/Kolkata**. Sources retrieved 23 October are used only for information available by the cutoff. Reference date: **19 October 2026**, ₹260.50 dated secondary closing-price reference, not a verified executable exchange quote. Five-year horizon ends 19 October 2031.\\n- Current issued shares **20,893,400**, authorized **25,000,000**, ₹10 face value; 400-share market lot. Listing 18 September 2026. The official NSE interoperability record corroborates security/share/lot data, **not an NSE listing or BSE tradeability**. [Share-capital reconciliation](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/reconcilation_share_capital_report.pdf), [dated secondary quote](https://shreni.in/company-profile/raksan-transformers).\\n- Consolidated Indian GAAP, not assumed Ind AS. Restated FY24–FY26 is the principal comparable accounting block; earlier original statements and their qualifications remain separate. Latest comparable FY27 interim/TTM and current cash-flow statement: **ND**, not estimated from PAT.\\n- Nominal equity hurdle **15% before investor taxes**, sensitivity 12%/18%. Separately assumed operating discount rate 15%, sensitivity 12%/18%; numerical coincidence does not make equity hurdle equal WACC by definition. Analytical cash floor ₹0.05 crore, stressed at ₹0.25/1/2 crore. No actual position supplied; liquidity reference **₹5 lakh**, not an allocation recommendation.\\n\\n| Gate | Status | Issue / resolution |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| G1 | Conditional | Recurring historical controls/RPT inconsistencies; no substantiated severe diversion or minority abuse established. Resolve with: Independent loan terms, commercial benchmarking and relevant-party recovery documentation. |\\n| G2 | Hold — unresolved | Material bank-return, restatement-vintage, related-loan and debt-table differences remain unresolved. Resolve with: Issuer/auditor reconciliation supported by bank statements and ledger extracts. |\\n| G3 | Hold — unresolved | March-to-October cash, IPO disbursement and committed drawable facilities not verified; scenarios can breach before IPO. This is not demonstrated actual insolvency. Resolve with: Verified dated cash/debt bridge, covenant/drawing-power and essential capex/WC funding. |\\n| G4 | Hold — unresolved | No complete official postlisting turnover/spread/circuit/restriction evidence. Resolve with: Official tradability, observed daily tape including no-trade sessions and executable lot/spread evidence. |\\n\\nConfidence: **Medium** on historical business, revenue decomposition and capital-return proxies; **Medium** on governance findings, with Low confidence that unresolved items are immaterial; **Low** on current cash/commitments, valuation and tradability. Overall investment confidence is therefore **Low**, not an average. A modeled historical cash breach is evidence that assumptions need validation, not proof that the company actually defaulted.\\n\\n\"","\"Scorecard and Calculation Audit\"","\"\\n| Measure | Raw | Final | Coverage | Gap / cap |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| BQS | 5.18 | 5.2 | 100.00% | No numerical override. |\\n| GQS | 6.50 | 5.0 | 100.00% | Persistent three-year weak cash realization triggers growth-quality cap5. |\\n| IAS | NS | NS | 45.00% | R/P/L unavailable; no weight redistribution. |\\n\\nExact BQS arithmetic: 0.80 GOV + 1.00 MOAT + 0.96 REV + 0.60 DUR + 0.72 CAP + 0.30 CASH + 0.40 BAL + 0.40 EXEC = **5.18**. GQS: 3.20 REV + 1.20 DUR + 0.90 EARN + 0.90 CAP + 0.30 CASH = **6.50**, capped at **5.00** because poor realization persists across three profitable years. This is not a penalty for expansion capex: capex is investing cash flow and cannot explain weak CFO.\\n\\nIAS reuses unrounded final BQS: 0.25×5.18 + 0.20×4 = **2.095 known contribution**; R/P/L missing weight **0.55**; coverage **45%**. Exact mathematical missing-data bound **[2.645, 7.595]**, not a confidence interval, valuation range or rankable score. No midpoint, renormalization or hidden haircut. Neither governance nor funding numerical failure override is applied because an evidenced severe failure is not established. Gate holds nevertheless preclude a favorable investment classification.\\n\\n| Factor | Score | Confidence | Evidence and contrary view |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| GOV | 4 | Medium | Historical audit qualifications and FY22 missing verification documentation are recurrent. SHR related purchases44.70cr plus terms-undefined advance1.42cr and bank-return discrepancies require scrutiny. Contrary: FY26 unmodified audit/effective IFC and later physical verification are improvements; no severe diversion established. [audit_old, rpt, bank_returns, audit_current] |\\n| MOAT | 5 | Medium | BIS/BEE qualification and in-house testing support participation. Two operating plants and repeat government utility customers demonstrate useful execution capability. Contrary: Lowest-bid tenders, weak bargaining and 2019 temporary exclusion prevent a durable-pricing-moat conclusion. [qualification_execution, prospectus] |\\n| REV | 8 | Medium | Scored window FY23–FY26 reported consolidated nominal revenue72.367795→363.1082cr, CAGR71.20%; not organic. Removing new FY26 trading gives endpoint337.7289cr and CAGR67.11%, still≥30% band. Manufactured transformer revenue160.19→322.53→336.52cr; trading separately removed. Physical distribution output822278→1375253KVA and power305.85→1285MVA support real expansion. Contrary: Latest manufactured sales growth4.34%, versus12.00% headline growth; five-year FY21 standalone/COVID series is context only, not the scored basis. Original/restated GAAP and unseparated price/service/mix limit confidence. Starting three-year ≥30% schedule9, limited to8 by Medium-confidence ceiling; no second discretionary haircut. [prospectus, audit2023] |\\n| DUR | 6 | Medium | June2026 confirmed order estimate329.68cr and83orders provides specific demand visibility. New project adds1900MVA power and704MVA inverter-duty capacity, planned December2026. Contrary: Tenders can cancel/defer; 58.56% UP revenue and new capacity qualification/commissioning not yet achieved. [prospectus, capacity] |\\n| CAP | 6 | Medium | FY24–26 observed incremental NOPAT exceeds incremental invested capital cost benchmark. Expanded power mix and utilization show existing assets earning more. Contrary: Prior margin/utilization improvement is not new-project IRR; ₹72.58cr project plus higher working capital means reinvestment returns not yet proven, especially with restatement/capital-payable bridge limits. [prospectus, capacity] |\\n| CASH | 3 | Medium | FY24–26 CFO/PAT ratio of sums≈0.45, not average of annual ratios. Receivables rose20.12→73.21cr and original/recast FCF remains thin/negative cumulatively. Contrary: CFO stayed positive across all three restated years and improvedFY26; growth explains assets, not automatic cash discipline. Poor realization persists across three profitable years, so GQS cap5 applies. [prospectus] |\\n| BAL | 5 | Medium | September fresh IPO gross120.47cr, net modeled108.74cr, substantially increases funding. March debt20.74cr is below one year EBITDA, with no reported default. Contrary: Net proceeds earmarked for capex/WC/debt, almost no March free cash, callable CC, guarantee commitments and June debt-total discrepancy constrain stress resilience. [prospectus, allotment, debt, guarantees] |\\n| EXEC | 5 | Medium | Physical throughput and power-transformer mix increased sharplyFY24–FY25. FY26 plant utilization exceeds90% for both main product classes. Contrary: Delay penalties recur; new plant promised December2026 is not delivered as of cutoff; 2019 qualification exclusion remains part of history. [prospectus, capacity, qualification_execution] |\\n| EARN | 6 | Medium | FY26 restated operating EBITDA growth is largely operating rather than other-income driven. Owners PAT improved20.38→33.60cr despite IPO-equivalent EPS denominator dilution. Contrary: Margin expansion while manufactured growth slows, original-to-restated PAT adjustment and weak cash conversion reduce durability; CFO concern scored separately inCASH. [prospectus, audit2026c] |\\n| R | NS | Low | Complete funded and unfunded counterfactual paths built. Base pre-entry/intraperiod cash can breach before IPO even with positive terminal accounting cash. Contrary: Current October funding/timing not verified; cash-cleared conditional branches are not a defensible unconditional return estimate. [model, debt] |\\n| D | 4 | Medium | Guarantee/receivable/working-capital/capex stresses can produce a cash shortfall. Whole-share rescues consume bounded bank/equity capacity, are not assured. Contrary: Fresh equity and tangible operating capacity provide some cushion; stress breach is not evidence of actual insolvency. [model, guarantees] |\\n| P | NS | Low | Reference market cap and reported multiples are calculated. Earned terminal value requires reinvestment and self-funding, not arbitrary PE. Contrary: Entry cash/commitments unreconciled and conditional terminal results cannot establish a supported valuation cushion. [model, debt] |\\n| L | NS | Low | 400share lot verified; reference cost104200rupees. ListingSeptember18 leaves short trading history. Contrary: Official postlisting turnover, spread, circuit/restriction state not established. Missing observations are ND, prelisting NA. [market, capital_reconciliation] |\\n\\nFactors use the same canonical values across scores. REV starts at 9 on the ≥30% historical growth schedule and is limited to 8 by Medium confidence/relevant-history limits, not reduced twice for the same limitation. CAP and EXEC ±1-point sensitivity produces BQS 4.98–5.38; GQS remains capped at 5 because CASH stays 3. These are judgment sensitivities, not different factual gate conclusions. Full factors, contributions, bounds and nine perturbations are machine-readable.\\n\\n\"","\"Business Overview\"","\"\\nRaksan earns manufacturing revenue from distribution and power transformers, plus repair/service/other activity and FY26 trading. FY26 product revenue includes distribution ₹233.0351 crore, power ₹100.1422 crore and other ₹29.9309 crore. Distribution transformers connect local distribution networks; higher-capacity power transformers address utility/industrial projects. Manufacturing requires conductive metals, electrical steel, insulation, testing and customer acceptance; revenue is not pure engineering value added.\\n\\nGovernment customers represented **50.73%** of FY26 sales versus **72.99%** in FY25. Uttar Pradesh contributed **58.56%**; six states together **97.13%**. A lower government percentage does not demonstrate broad geographic diversification. Tender awards, manufacturing, inspection/dispatch, billing, collection and release of guarantees/retention are different milestones. Accounting sales can therefore grow before discretionary cash. [Prospectus, business/customer/geography disclosures, printed pp112–129](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nThe consolidated Haryana Power Industries **partnership** was controlled from November 2015; ownership increased from 95% to 99.99% on 19 May 2025 for ₹0.0437 crore minority consideration. FY26 external revenue was nil and loss ₹0.1592 crore. That ownership change is not the source of headline manufacturing growth. A separate same-name HUF/proprietary related counterparty must not be conflated with the consolidated entity. [Prospectus, group and related-party notes](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n\"","\"Moat / Industry Position\"","\"\\n**Useful qualification and execution capability, not demonstrated durable pricing power.** ISO processes, BIS eligibility up to the disclosed distribution ratings, BEE efficiency ratings and internal testing facilitate approved-vendor participation. They do not eliminate competing qualified suppliers, lowest-price bidding, raw-material exposure, inspection failure or customer concentration. The issuer disclosed exclusion from three consecutive PVVNL tenders under a 20 June 2019 order. The business continued afterward, but the history demonstrates that eligibility is not permanent. [Prospectus, printed pp22,124](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nNo contract-level evidence establishes universal or timely copper/electrical-steel price pass-through. Price-escalation clauses can protect the ultimate invoice while still leaving a timing gap, excluded items, benchmark mismatch or tender-margin compression. Inventory and funding requirements remain even where eventual pass-through exists. The January 2026 rating supports business continuity but its liquidity forecast is not a bank commitment. [Infomerics, 13 January 2026](https://infomericstorage.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/pr_raksan_transformers_13jan26_8d9de3f012.pdf), [10 February 2025](https://www.infomerics.com/admin/uploads/pr-raksan-transformers-10feb25.pdf).\\n\\nEconomic comparators:\\n\\n- **Shilchar Technologies** is the stronger historical margin/export-diversification reference: FY25 revenue about ₹623 crore, approximately 30% EBITDA margin, 43% exports and stated net cash ₹91 crore. These are FY25 historical facts, not current comparable valuation inputs. They show that technology/product/customer mix and cash generation matter beyond generic transformer demand. [FY25 report, printed pp2–4,14–15](https://shilchar.com/upload/power_investor_relations/annual-report-2024-2025.pdf).\\n- **Supreme Power Equipment** offers a commissioning/qualification comparison. Its June 2026 release says February commissioning increased capacity from 2,500 to 9,000 MVA with capability up to 200 MVA/220kV. Those **9,000 MVA belong to Supreme, not Raksan**. Management's ₹500–550 crore full-utilization sales potential is not an independently verified revenue guarantee. Conflicting income/PAT labels in that release are not imported into a profitability ranking. [Exchange release, pp2–3](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/SPEL_01062026185238_SPELH2FY26PressRelease.pdf).\\n- **Marsons** is an issuer-selected peer with lower FY26 closing-equity RONW than Shilchar in the prospectus comparison. That one ratio does not establish lower total business quality. Its old annual-report link returned 404; a fresh independently reconciled audit comparison remains incomplete.\\n\\nThe prospectus peer P/Es, 49.63x Marsons, 29.47x Shilchar and 27.75x Supreme, use **28 August 2026** prices and their own share/earnings bases. They are neither current comparable quotes nor permission to apply a 30x exit multiple to Raksan. [Prospectus, printed p96](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n\"","\"Revenue Growth & Scale\"","\"\\nOriginal audited history, retained without splicing into the restated cash/capital series:\\n\\n| FY | Scope | Revenue | Owners PAT | CFO | Cash capex |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2020 | Standalone, FY21 comparative; pre-restatement | 61.61 | 1.76 | ND | ND |\\n| 2021 | Standalone original, qualified | 34.22 | 0.07 | 1.43 | 4.01 |\\n| 2022 | Consolidated original FY23 comparative, uncorrected AS15/MSME | 58.26 | 0.74 | -1.07 | 0.04 |\\n| 2023 | Consolidated original, subject-to AS15/MSME | 72.37 | 3.47 | 5.59 | 0.33 |\\n\\nFY20 is an earlier comparison year, not a seventh fully reconstructed annual cash-flow record. FY21 is a COVID trough and standalone; FY22–23 consolidated comparatives carry old audit/control limitations. Headline historical CAGR: **3y 2023–2026: 71.20% (₹72.37→363.11 crore); 5y 2021–2026: 60.38% (₹34.22→363.11 crore)**. A reliable ten-year CAGR is ND. These are nominal revenue CAGRs, not organic volume or intrinsic-value growth. **The scored REV window is FY23–FY26 reported consolidated revenue, ₹72.367795→₹363.1082 crore, approximately71.20% CAGR.** The same controlled-subsidiary perimeter is used, but the old original/restated GAAP qualifications limit confidence. The FY21 standalone/COVID trough makes the five-year series context only, not the primary scoring basis. As a robustness check, removing new FY26 trading gives endpoint₹337.7289 crore and approximately67.11% nominal CAGR, still within the same ≥30% starting band. This check is not a complete constant-price manufactured-sales CAGR: earlier service, price and mix are not fully separable. The FY24–FY26 physical-output evidence below supports genuine manufacturing expansion, without relabeling all nominal growth organic.\\n\\n| FY | Revenue addition | YoY |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 2021 | -27.39 | -44.46% |\\n| 2022 | 24.04 | 70.25% |\\n| 2023 | 14.11 | 24.22% |\\n| 2024 | 88.58 | 122.40% |\\n| 2025 | 163.26 | 101.44% |\\n| 2026 | 38.90 | 12.00% |\\n\\nThe manufactured-sales bridge is more informative: FY24 **₹160.1914 crore**, FY25 **₹322.5265 crore**, FY26 **₹336.5174 crore**. FY26 trading sales **₹25.3793 crore** on purchases **₹25.2732 crore** imply only **₹0.1061 crore** gross spread before other costs. Manufacturing increased ₹13.9909 crore, **4.34%**, while headline revenue increased ₹38.8984 crore, approximately **12.00%**. Trading alone contributes ₹25.3793 crore; the residual other-sales mix declines about ₹0.4718 crore. It is wrong to call all headline growth organic manufacturing expansion. [Prospectus, revenue and purchases notes, printed pp193–196](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nPhysical output corroborates real prior growth: distribution **822,278 → 1,175,472 → 1,375,253 KVA** and power **305.85 → 1,156.75 → 1,285 MVA** in FY24–FY26. FY26 growth includes mix and pricing, but contract-level price/volume decomposition is ND. Distribution output grew about17% and power about11%, while aggregate manufactured value grew4.34%; changing mix/realizations therefore matter. No independently measured market-share gain is asserted. [Prospectus, capacity/production tables](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n\"","\"Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\"","\"\\nAt 30 June 2026 the issuer reported **83 confirmed orders, estimated unexecuted value ₹329.6792 crore**. The figure is not guaranteed near-term sales or cash: escalation, freight/taxes, delivery changes, cancellation, inspections and collections affect conversion. No customer-level cash-secured backlog reconciliation was located. Larger utility investment is an accessible demand opportunity, not proof Raksan wins a fixed market share. [Prospectus, order-book disclosures](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nExisting annual capacity is **1,500 MVA distribution + 1,350 MVA power = 2,850 MVA**; FY26 utilization91.68%/95.18%. The new project adds **1,900 MVA power +704 MVA inverter duty**, yielding **5,454 MVA** combined capacity, not9,000. Distribution capacity does not increase. Target commissioning and Consent to Operate: **December2026**, a management milestone not delivered as of cutoff. Capacity does not equal customer-approved saleable output. [Capacity certificate](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/proposed_capacity_post_expansion.pdf), [Prospectus, objects/business](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nProject budget **₹72.5843 crore**, already-paid **₹10.4477 crore**, IPO-funded remainder **₹62.1366 crore**. The engineer certificate shows₹72.5837 crore, a ₹0.0006 crore rounding/estimate difference retained rather than hidden. Land is not included in this incremental project budget. Incremental sales capacity near₹600 crore is an analytical mix/price approximation, not issuer guidance: FY26 power revenue/MVA is about₹0.0779 crore, and distribution differs materially. Beyond₹600 crore sales the model charges₹0.35 of additional fixed-capital investment per incremental revenue rupee, plus working capital and restricted deposits. The ratio roughly links project cost per new MVA to FY26 power realizations; new product mix, qualification and execution can invalidate it.\\n\\nGQS6.50 raw does not mean growth is already self-funded. GQS is capped5.00 by persistent CASH3. Existing margin/utilization improvement can lift observed incremental ROIC without proving attractive returns on the proposed plant. Cash collection and capital efficiency, not a growing order headline alone, must earn an improved score.\\n\\n\"","\"Management, Governance & Execution\"","\"\\nThe original audit record was inspected across FY21/FY22 standalone, FY23–FY26 consolidated and FY26 standalone, including annexures and notes, rather than relying only on the IPO summary.\\n\\n- **FY21** explicitly qualified unaccounted AS15 gratuity and MSMED supplier interest. Similar issues recur through subsequent early reports. **FY22 CARO** says PPE records/physical-verification and inventory-verification documentation were not produced. FY22 March bank debtors were₹12.277766 crore versus books₹15.267245 crore, difference₹2.989479 crore; stock book comparison was not available. [FY21 audit p1](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2021.pdf), [FY22 annexures pp7–8,16](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2022.pdf).\\n- **FY26** original opinion is unmodified, IFC described effective and audit-trail operation/preservation reported. Later PPE/inventory verification is a real improvement, not erasure of historical limitations. The original FY25 first-page opinion appears unmodified while the prospectus describes FY24/FY25 modified reports; the wording conflict remains unresolved. [FY26 standalone audit](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf), [prospectus pp163–164](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n- **Recurring bank-return differences remain material.** FY26 Q4 book/bank inventory₹25.9117/20.2383 crore; receivables₹73.2119/60.4163; payables₹43.5185/37.2298. Differences₹5.6734/12.7956/6.2887 crore. Explanations mention unclosed quarters, year-end adjustments, excluded WIP and net advances. They are not transaction-level reconciliations or evidence of unrestricted cash. [FY26 standalone Annexure C](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf), [prospectus pp178–179](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n- Related-party **SHR Powers** purchases₹44.7038 crore, sales₹2.2731 crore and closing advance₹1.4209 crore are significant. FY26 Annexure D describes an advance in the nature of a loan with undefined terms; CAROiii(c–e) cannot comment on repayment/overdues, whileiii(f) is inconsistent about unspecified-term related advances. Demand signed terms, purpose, arm's-length benchmarking and recovery, not a presumption of theft. Sanjeev remuneration₹1.50 crore plus₹0.0125 crore bonus/leave, Dievam salary₹0.48 crore and related rent₹0.468 crore are disclosed. [Prospectus pp56–58,199,204](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf), [standalone Annexure D](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf).\\n- A proposed related-property sale carries₹0.31 crore advance and December2027 deadline. Price-unit wording is ambiguous; no future sale cash is assumed. Missing old ROC forms, minutes and transfer deeds plus filing errors are disclosed. No material criminal litigation or proven severe minority abuse is established by the reviewed evidence. [Prospectus pp28–29 and related-party notes](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\n| Dated commitment / result | Evidence as of cutoff | Interpretation |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| FY24–FY26 throughput expansion | Power output305.85→1,285MVA | Demonstrated execution, not merely announced capacity |\\n| FY25/FY26 deliveries | Late-delivery charges₹3.2017/2.6384crore | Recurring cost, not penalty-free execution |\\n| December2026 new-plant target | Not yet commissioned by20October | Remains forecast; test0/6/12-month delay |\\n| FY26 AGM timing | Extension to5December2026 | Track completion; extension itself is not fraud |\\n\\n[Late-delivery/warranty notes and project schedule](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf), [AGM extension](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/agm_extention_intimation.pdf).\\n\\n\"","\"Financial Forensics\"","\"\\nRestated consolidated history, ₹crore, Indian GAAP. Operating EBIT = PBT + finance cost − other income; operating EBITDA adds D&A. This removes non-operating income, not every possible normalization. No undisclosed margin uplift is added. PAT and CFO use matching consolidated scope; owners PAT drives EPS.\\n\\n| FY | Revenue | Operating EBITDA | Owners PAT | CFO | Cash capex | FCF | Debt | Free cash | IC proxy |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2024 | 160.95 | 10.93 | 7.59 | 7.43 | 2.49 | 4.94 | 9.81 | 4.64 | 29.76 |\\n| 2025 | 324.21 | 29.78 | 20.38 | 5.36 | 27.63 | -22.27 | 23.51 | 0.21 | 68.72 |\\n| 2026 | 363.11 | 47.10 | 33.60 | 14.89 | 11.30 | 3.58 | 20.74 | 0.23 | 103.10 |\\n\\nThree-year CFO/PAT 44.95%; cash-interest-adjusted 41.59%; reported FCF sum ₹-13.75 crore; after capital advances ₹-15.99 crore; two-year incremental ROIC 35.97%.\\n\\nThe cash issue is receivables and operating reinvestment, not merely capex. Receivables rose₹20.1219→52.0221→73.2119crore; inventory₹19.4491→21.2447→25.9117; payables₹26.6862→42.4227→43.5185. FY26's₹21.1898crore AR increase exceeds CFO₹14.8853crore. Average AR/total-revenue days is a labeled proxy for credit-revenue days. Comparable gross-profit, credit-purchases and asset-level maintenance splits areND where not unambiguously separated; no synthetic gross margin is substituted for disclosed operating EBITDA. Contract assets/retention are not independently disclosed enough to assert a clean cash-conversion cycle; inventory/payable days with compatible purchasing denominators remain ND rather than mixing misleading denominators.\\n\\n| FY | NOPAT at25% tax | IC | ROIC average | 1y incremental ROIC | Average AR days proxy |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2024 | 7.91 | 29.76 | ND | ND | ND |\\n| 2025 | 21.62 | 68.72 | 43.90% | 35.18% | 40.61 |\\n| 2026 | 34.29 | 103.10 | 39.92% | 36.88% | 62.94 |\\n\\nIC funding-side bridge adds equity, NCI, funded debt, capital creditors, tax/financing/property-advance exclusions from operating liabilities, and subtracts available cash, DTA and non-operating investments. Restricted/security deposits remain operating invested capital, not debt-netting cash. FY26 direct asset-side IC: ONWC49.3075 + fixed/CWIP45.2435 + capital advances2.2439 + deposits6.3066 =₹103.1015crore, versus funding-side₹103.1013; ₹0.0002 rounding difference. FY24 payables components sum₹2,668.63 lakh versus printed₹2,668.62; this table uses the printed total. FY25 components sum₹4,242.27 lakh versus printed₹4,242.28; this table retains the component sum. Each ₹0.01 lakh difference is ₹0.0001 crore, explicitly retained rather than treated as a substantive reconciliation. Reconciled residual ONWC is also retained. NOPAT uses an explicit25% normalized operating tax assumption; actual taxes differ. Average-capital ROIC/ROCE differs from issuer closing-equity RONW. Three/five-year comparable incremental ROIC is **ND** because earlier capital classifications/qualifications are not reconciled, not because older evidence was ignored. Two-year incremental proxy is not marginal project IRR; utilization, product mix and margin improvement can dominate it. [Prospectus, statements/notes pp166–209](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nOriginal-vintage conflicts are explicit. FY26 original PAT₹33.3531→restated33.6048crore is bridged by removing₹0.2539prior-year tax and₹0.0022additional depreciation. CFO14.8871→14.8853, equity77.5941→77.4159; original investment property0.7883 disappears and PPE39.8193→40.5695. Reclassification net of accumulated depreciation is consistent with part of that movement but is not a complete issuer-certified balance bridge. FY25 original comparative PAT20.7637→20.3767 differs₹0.3870. Do not combine original equity with restated profits. FY23 reported cash₹8.323753 included₹7.267057restricted margin deposits: genuinely available cash₹1.056696. [FY26 original consolidated statements](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_consolidated_signed_2025_26.pdf), [FY23 consolidated](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2023.pdf).\\n\\n**IPO and debt bridge.** Pre-IPO16,480,600 shares + fresh4,412,800 =20,893,400; OFS1,100,000 transfers old holdings and supplies no corporate cash. At₹273, fresh gross₹120.46944crore less modeled issuer expenses₹11.7302 =₹108.73924net. Objects: capex62.1366, WC35, debt7.2834, GCP4.3192crore; ₹0.00004difference is rounding. Fresh issuance dilutes old proportional ownership by21.12%; 18:1 bonus is not economic dilution. Post-issue book before subsequent operating movements should add **net**, not gross proceeds:₹186.15514crore. Issuer gross-proceeds NAV is not net usable cash. The prospectus expressly reports no outstanding convertible instruments, warrants or conversion rights and no promoter/group pledge at its date. The30September shareholding reports promoter/group15,380,600shares (73.61%), including Sanjeev13,003,662 (62.24%); public26.39% is not equivalent to actively tradable free float after lock-ins. Future equity is explicit uncommitted scenario funding, not a disclosed planned issue. [30September shareholding](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/shareholding_pattern_bse_30.9.26.pdf). [Allotment](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/basis_of_allotment_advertisement.pdf), [prospectus capital/objects](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nMarch debt₹20.7364crore, free cash₹0.2257crore. June funded debt rows sum **₹29.7773crore**, not printed₹26.1274; ₹3.6499difference nearly equals the new May₹3.65LAP. March debt plus CC increase₹5.7219 and May draw equals₹30.1083. Model June principal₹0.3310reconciles the row sum, explicitly an **assumption**, not verified cash flow. Later principal₹0.18/month is separately stressed. Old LAP₹7.3648 differs from objects table₹7.4134. ₹22.5crore CC sanction, one-year/callable renewal and rating facilities are not verified October undrawn commitments. The model does not automatically roll the facility. [Prospectus pp90,211–213](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf).\\n\\nGuarantees₹17.4788crore versus₹4.1673FY25 and capital commitments₹46.7575crore matter beyond reported funded debt. Deposits₹6.3066cannot be spent freely. FY26 warranty settlements₹0.9058crore, closing provision₹0.4744crore; no unsupported claim that provision covers every future warranty. Retention, guarantee-release and procurement-price protection schedules are ND. Rent remains an operating cost; no unverified lease capitalization or property-sale proceeds are fabricated.\\n\\n\"","\"Valuation & Market Expectations\"","\"\\nReference calculations, not current enterprise value: **market_cap=544.27; pe_postipo_equivalent=16.20; ev_march_debt_cash_reference=564.78; ev_ebitda_march_reference=11.99; postipo_equivalent_eps=16.08; book_march=77.42; proforma_book_after_net_fresh_issue=186.16; pb_net_proceeds_proforma=2.92**. Post-IPO equivalent EPS uses current issued shares against FY26 owners earnings, not the smaller historical IPO EPS denominator. Current October EV is **ND** until cash/debt/use-of-proceeds reconciles. Apparently modest historical P/E is not automatically cheap after new capex, cash retention, minority/control risk and execution limitations.\\n\\nThe linked model begins at audited31March2026, with seven dated pre-entry buckets through19October, then60monthly post-entry buckets and12monthly terminal-continuation buckets. Each bucket exposes customer receipts, cash costs, WC, restricted deposits, taxes, interest, capex, repayments and remaining receipts. Revenues are annual trajectories, not a quarterly annualization. Project attribution of March CWIP/advances, cash spent by entry₹25crore and IPO cash date30September are assumptions with sensitivity. Original capital-payable settlement is separated from new project assets. Opening fixed₹41.5881crore plus project₹5.8993crore totals₹47.4874: capital advances₹2.2439 are outside the₹45.2435fixed/CWIP figure and included once, not deducted twice. Intangible development₹0.0793 remains inside the modeled fixed approximation; the3.5%depreciation is an explicit estimate, not a purported asset-level issuer schedule. All initial balances, code and formulas are included.\\n\\nAssumptions (not guidance): bear sales₹370/380/410/450/490crore and margins7.5/7.5/8/8.5/8.5%; base₹450/525/610/690/760 and12/12/11.5/11/11%; bull₹520/650/800/950/1,100 and13.5/13/12.5/12/12%. Pre-entry annual sales360/400/430 and margins9/12/13%. Before commissioning, post-entry annualized revenue is capped₹400crore without later catch-up. Bear capex25%overrun and12-month delay. AR110/80/70days; inventory11/9/8%revenue, payables8/10.5/11%; cash operating costs paid before the last10%of receipts. This ordering is a stress convention, not a verified monthly settlement sequence.\\n\\n| Case | First cash breach | Entry cash / debt | Terminal cash / debt | Conditional return | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| bear_none | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹8.21 | 26.27 / 21.84 | -8.06 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bear_bounded_optional | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹8.21 | 26.27 / 21.84 | -8.06 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| base_none | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹1.71 | 70.77 / 21.84 | 100.15 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| base_bounded_optional | m-7 net_working_capital_investment; shortfall₹1.71 | 70.77 / 21.84 | 100.15 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bull_none | m-7 cash_taxes; shortfall₹0.84 | 86.50 / 21.84 | 64.03 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n| bull_bounded_optional | m-7 cash_taxes; shortfall₹0.84 | 86.50 / 21.84 | 64.03 / 0.00 | NS | Cash failure; terminal balance is counterfactual |\\n\\n**Every ordinary bear/base/bull path breaches before IPO under its timing assumptions. No ordinary IRR is reported.** Later positive cash is a counterfactual rollforward, not survival. Post-entry optional funding is prohibited from curing that earlier failure. Higher cash-floor stress can fail at the audited opening itself; that result is retained, not silently recentered to a cash-rich IPO date.\\n\\nOptional rescue, only before a new post-entry breach: maximum₹20crore gross bank draw at12%, immediate draw-month interest,12-month grace then36-month repayment; maximum₹40crore gross equity at₹208.40,3%fees, **integer whole shares**, bounded by25million authorized capital and4,106,600new-share ceiling. Draw/issuance totals remain bounded even after prior debt amortizes. This is not committed finance. Existing debt runs off without automatic CC renewal. Optional branches never receive ordinary IRR.\\n\\nFor diagnosis only, a separate conditional branch assumes all pre-entry monthly receipts arrive before costs, AR70days and bull pre-entry activity. This optimistic cash-clear bridge is **not observed October cash**. It reveals which post-entry economics survive instead of falsely rehabilitating the main failed paths:\\n\\n| AR days / margin / funding | Bank / equity gross | Dilution | Survival | Conditional IRR | Counterfactual terminal price |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 80_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 144.97 |\\n| 80_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 129.22 |\\n| 80_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 219.89 |\\n| 80_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 197.06 |\\n| 80_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | True | 3.05% | 302.68 |\\n| 80_.12_bounded_optional | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | True | 3.05% | 302.68 |\\n| 100_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 134.45 |\\n| 100_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 122.90 |\\n| 100_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 209.36 |\\n| 100_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 191.07 |\\n| 100_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 284.28 |\\n| 100_.12_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 257.27 |\\n| 120_.08_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 123.92 |\\n| 120_.08_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 113.50 |\\n| 120_.10_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 198.84 |\\n| 120_.10_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 182.11 |\\n| 120_.12_none | 0.00 / 0.00 | 0.00% | False | NS | 273.75 |\\n| 120_.12_bounded_optional | 20.00 / 40.00 | 8.41% | False | NS | 250.65 |\\n\\nEarned terminal EV is next-year FCFF/(WACC−g), not an arbitrary exit P/E. FCFF deducts25%operating tax, maintenance at1.25×modeled D&A, fixed-capital growth, working-capital/restricted-deposit growth, **and growth of required operating liquidity**. D&A is3.5%of operating fixed capital; maintenance1.0/1.25/1.5× and debt rates10/11.45/14%are tested. Required operating cash reserve is solved over every unlevered continuation prefix with a growing reserve; g×reserve is segregated and deducted from FCFF. A distinct cash continuation pays all remaining debt and declining interest. Debt is deducted **once** from EV plus cash above the operating reserve, not also hidden inside the valuation reserve. No dividends or property-sale windfalls assumed.\\n\\nSelected branch: conditional_preentry_clear_stress_80_.12_none. Survives modeled cash tests, not observed entry funding.\\n\\n| WACC / perpetual growth | 2% | 4% | 6% |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 12.00% | 382.66 | 413.23 | 464.17 |\\n| 15.00% | 296.29 | 302.68 | 311.90 |\\n| 18.00% | 242.31 | 239.51 | 235.77 |\\n\\nConditional entry prices for that selected branch, not a supported unconditional fair-value range:\\n\\n| Hurdle | Conditional entry price | After2% entry and2% exit friction |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 12.00% | 171.75 | 165.01 |\\n| 15.00% | 150.48 | 144.58 |\\n| 18.00% | 132.30 | 127.12 |\\n\\nThe2%entry/2%exit friction example is an assumption, not measured spreads or an execution promise. Discount/growth matrix, margin/growth grid, AR60/80/100/120days, front receipts85/90/95/100%, terminal timing80/90/100%, capex/delay, retention0/2.5/5%ofsales, CCrunoff1/13/25months, IPOdelay, principal bridge, guarantees0/10/100%, openingproject attribution and rescue-price/cap sensitivities are retained. No rerating multiple is needed to earn value; weak FCFF or inability to continue suppresses return scoreability.\\n\\nReverse expectations use the cash-clear conditional history, starting revenue₹400crore, revenue CAGR−20%to100%grid, then24bisections only across adjacent surviving sign changes. A failed intermediate candidate invalidates that bracket, rather than being assigned a return. **All candidate paths, including failures, are retained.**\\n\\n| Funding | Hurdle | Candidates | Roots | Scope |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| none | 12.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 15.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 18.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 37.97% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| none | 58.49% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 12.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 15.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 18.00% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 37.97% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n| bounded_optional | 58.49% | 25 | No bracketed surviving root | Conditional cash-clear pre-entry only |\\n\\nNo bracketed root means none found in the stated surviving domain, not impossibility for all conceivable financing or assumptions. The unconstrained algebraic root of a failed cash path is not an investable expectation.\\n\\nLiquidity: a400-share lot costs₹104,200; four lots₹416,800, five₹521,000beforefees. For the₹5lakhreference, actual sizing is discrete. Official20/60-session turnover means/medians, postlisting zero-trade counts, spread and current restrictions areND; dates before18September areNA, not zero volume. The dated secondary19October volume60,800is a one-day cross-check only. Liquidation days at2/5/10%participation remainND without the prescribed conservative mean/median daily value. L and G4 cannot be cleared from one active day or the existence of an interoperability record.\\n\\n\"","\"Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\"","\"\\n**High impairment risk under linked stress, with uncertain actual funding resilience.** Tender deferral/lost qualification reduces throughput; fixed costs and raw-material mismatch depress margins; slower collections and retention increase funded WC; project overrun consumes earmarked IPO cash; a callable CC renewal or guarantee call then arrives before collection. Lenders and suppliers have prior claims; existing shareholders face dilution, forced asset realization or impaired future earning power. A temporary quoted drawdown is different from this funding/earning-capacity impairment.\\n\\nBear adds₹1.74788crore guarantee cash call (10%ofMarchguarantees),₹3.660595ARnoncollection (5%ofMarchAR),₹1.4209relatedadvance loss and25%projectoverrun. Full-guarantee sensitivity is also retained. These are linked analytical losses, not assertions of existing fraud/default. The exact ordinary bear price loss is **NS** because its cash bridge fails; printing a normal target-price return would conceal the financing problem. Conditional terminal-price diagnostics are not claim-recovery estimates.\\n\\nThe most important thesis-break variable is **verified customer cash collection sufficient to fund essential WC and commissioning without unfavorable rescue**. Strongest opposing evidence to this cautious view: a profitable real manufacturer, high utilization, improving reported CFO, fresh equity and an unmodifiedFY26audit. None independently resolves the dated liquidity/control evidence gaps. A documented serious minority-abuse finding would change G1 to evidenced failure; ordinary volatility alone would not.\\n\\n\"","\"5× / 10× Feasibility\"","\"\\nFivefold price growth over five years requires about37.97%annualized; tenfold58.49%. Per-share outcomes depend on revenue×margin×valuation **divided by diluted shares**, not merely enterprise sales. The reverse tests above include both multiples, with every cash/funding path retained. Optional equity can raise enterprise survival probability while reducing existing-holder value. A lower terminal capitalization is covered by18%discount/2%growth, not by pretending a high peer P/E persists.\\n\\nThe commissioned capacity/mix approximation is near₹600crore annual sales; larger revenues require new fixed investment, WC, qualification, customers and cash collection. No verified market-share bridge supports several multiples of that capacity or repeated capital raising on favorable terms. **5×/10× are speculative / unsupported as current investment theses**, even if a conditional numerical root appears in an optimistic financing domain. There is no defensible success probability or price target.\\n\\n\"","\"Monitoring Plan\"","\"\\nResearch checkpoints only; no automatic trade or reminder is created.\\n\\n| KPI / event | Baseline | Warning / investigation | Thesis-break / clearance evidence | Review source / timing |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Cash and IPO use | Marchfreecash0.2257; netfresh108.73924 | Disbursement cannot reconcile to banks | Essential payments unsupported without rescue; clear only with dated bank/ledger bridge | First post-IPO results/use-of-proceeds report |\\n| Manufactured growth | FY26growth4.34% | Headline growth again led by thin-spread trading | Manufacturing stagnation alongside financed expansion | Each comparable half/full year |\\n| Collection | AR73.2119; CFO/PAT3y≈45% | AR growth again exceeds manufacturing sales/cash growth | Material noncollection or unexplained receivable ageing | Audited ageing/collections; at least half-yearly |\\n| Bank reconciliations | MarchARdifference12.7956 | New material unreconciled returns | Evidence of deliberate material misstatement, or verified remediation to clear G2 | Auditor/issuer Annexure C and bank evidence |\\n| Plant | Dec2026 target; added2604MVA | No permits/testing/customer qualification at target | Costs rise without viable financed commissioning | Completion certificate/Consent to Operate/customer approval |\\n| Capital returns | ICproxy103.1013 | Margin gains do not translate into cash after full capital | Persistently sub-hurdle normalized incremental economics | Full-year cohort and capital bridge |\\n| Guarantees/warranty | Guarantees17.4788; settlement0.9058 | Calls/LDs materially exceed historic pattern | Calls cannot be funded or qualification lost | Utility/issuer disclosures and audited notes |\\n| Related advance | SHR1.4209; undefined terms | No signed repayment/commercial explanation | Evidenced abuse or unrecoverable material related exposure | RPT approvals, loan documents, collections |\\n| Debt | June row-sum29.7773; CCcallable | Renewal/covenants/drawing power unavailable | Verified default or unfinanceable essential obligations | Bank/rating/issuer filings |\\n| Tradability | 400sharelot; short history | One-sided circuits, sparse tape, restrictions | Effectively no executable reference-position exit | Official trading/restriction data before any implementation |\\n\\nThresholds require investigation and causal evidence, not an automatic buy/sell response to a single number.\\n\\n\"","\"Final Classification & Conditional Action\"","\"\\n**Hold — unresolved; research priority only.** Historical quality is mixed (BQS5.18), growth quality limited by cash realization (finalGQS5.00), and IAS isNS. Put this record in **Pending evidence for all batch lists** until critical gate evidence is resolved; do not force it into an ordinal rank or portray it as proven governance failure. It fails compounder requirements independently on quality, cash, moat, governance and unresolved gates.\\n\\nA lower quote alone cannot resolve G2/G3/G4. A better investment assessment requires the missing dated funding/control evidence first, then supported operating assumptions, a fully surviving ordinary return model and implementable liquidity. Conditional prices in section10 are research diagnostics, not instructions. Existing-holder suitability, portfolio concentration, taxes and a specific reduction/exit count are not assessed because no holding information was supplied.\\n\\n\"","\"Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\"","\"\\nEvidence types: **V** primary historical disclosures; **C** exact calculations from identified inputs; **M** management plans/order estimates; **A** analyst forecasts, timing, recovery/funding and valuation assumptions. Primary historical tables areV; score arithmetic, ratios and bridges areC; December commissioning/order realization areM; all post-March operational cash paths and terminal values areA/C. Confidence is attached by subject and canonical factor, not implied by a long source list.\\n\\n| ID | Document / link | Cutoff / scope |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| prospectus | [Prospectus](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/prospectus.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2021 | [Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2021](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2021.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2022 | [Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2022](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/audited_financial_statements_march_31_2022.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2023 | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2023](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2023.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2024c | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2024](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2024.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2025c | [Consolidated Audited Financial Statements 31.03.2025](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/consolidated_audited_financial_statements_march_31_2025.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2026c | [Consolidated Financial Statements 2025-26](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_consolidated_signed_2025_26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| audit2026s | [Standalone Financial Statements 2025-26](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/raksan_fs_standalone_signed_2025_26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| capacity | [Proposed Capacity Post Expansion](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/proposed_capacity_post_expansion.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| shareholding | [Shareholding Pattern BSE 30.09.2026](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/shareholding_pattern_bse_30.9.26.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| capital_reconciliation | [Reconcilation Share Capital Report](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/reconcilation_share_capital_report.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| allotment | [Basis of Allotment Advertisement](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/basis_of_allotment_advertisement.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| agm | [AGM Extention Intimation](https://raksantransformers.com/assets/pdf/agm_extention_intimation.pdf) | Historical/audit evidence; source locations in audit_evidence and report. Retrieval after cutoff does not authorize postcutoff events. |\\n| rating2026 | [Infomerics January13 2026 credit rationale](https://infomericstorage.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/pr_raksan_transformers_13jan26_8d9de3f012.pdf) | StandaloneBBB/Positive,A3+; source opinion, not bank commitment. |\\n| rating2025 | [Infomerics February10 2025 credit rationale](https://www.infomerics.com/admin/uploads/pr-raksan-transformers-10feb25.pdf) | Earlier orderbook and standalone trajectory; not spliced with restated consolidated financials. |\\n| market_secondary | [Shreni datedOctober19 Raksan market reference](https://shreni.in/company-profile/raksan-transformers) | Price260.50, not execution or official liquidity certification. |\\n| peer_shilchar_2025 | [Shilchar FY25 annual report](https://shilchar.com/upload/power_investor_relations/annual-report-2024-2025.pdf) | Historical FY25 operating comparison, not latest trading or valuation. |\\n| peer_supreme_2026 | [Supreme June1 2026 results and operational release](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/SPEL_01062026185238_SPELH2FY26PressRelease.pdf) | Management commissioning/capacity and qualification comparison; conflicting income/PAT labels not used in valuation. |\\n| nse_interop_20261019 | [NSE October19 2026 interoperability security master](https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/cm/interop/NSE_CM_security_19102026.csv.gz) | Two RAKSAN$ rows match ISIN,400sharelot and20,893,400issued shares. No BSE trading/price/circuit conclusion from metadata. |\\n\\nSource locations and transcribed contradictions are retained in the audit ledger; exact original/restated vintages in historical inputs. Issuer statements are generally₹lakh converted by100 to₹crore, with visible rounding differences. Full PDF/OCR binaries are intentionally not redistributed. This package is standalone for reconstructing every research result, not a substitute for reading the linked originals. Peer statements are comparative context, not independently completed peer scoring.\\n\\nMaterial unanswered questions: customer-specific pass-through/retention and collection schedules; actual IPO cash dates/spending; current unrestricted cash and drawable credit; bank-return ledger reconciliation; original-to-restated balance bridge; related-advance terms/recovery; plant permit/qualification milestones; outstanding guarantee release timing; official trade tape and restrictions. These gaps have explicit score/gate consequences, not invented neutral values.\\n\\nReproducibility: **164 unique complete parameter paths; 143 named tests; 250 reverse evaluations, including every failed candidate.** Content-hashed parameter paths and terminal-continuation references preserve all rows losslessly. `canonical.json` is the computational record; `scenario_summary.csv` is a view, not an alternative model. Decimal arithmetic retains unrounded calculations; displayed scores use half-up one-decimal rounding. The external-baseline recovery workflow authenticates every authored input/code file, deletes all generated outputs and attestations, and reconstructs identical outputs without PDFs, network, helpers or private identities. Internal numerical validation is not issuer verification.\\n\\nUpdate record,23October2026: first complete v3 research for the20Octobercutoff; original/restated conflicts, June-debt summation and growing terminal liquidity costs incorporated. No prior v2.2 score is silently compared. No postcutoff operational event or later price is used. Research is conditional and informational, not a financial transaction or personalized allocation recommendation.\\n\"","\"heading_start\"","\"body_start\"","\"original_heading\"","1378","\"## 1. Executive Verdict\\n\"","1427","4616","\"## 2. Research Header, Gates and Data Confidence\\n\"","4654","11482","\"## 3. Scorecard and Calculation Audit\\n\"","11506","13131","\"## 4. Business Overview\\n\"","13162","16258","\"## 5. Moat / Industry Position\\n\"","16287","19446","\"## 6. Revenue Growth & Scale\\n\"","19489","21782","\"## 7. Growth Quality & Reinvestment Runway\\n\"","21823","25699","\"## 8. Management, Governance & Execution\\n\"","25725","32326","\"## 9. Financial Forensics\\n\"","32365","42264","\"## 10. Valuation & Market Expectations\\n\"","42303","43917","\"## 11. Bear Case & Permanent-Loss Path\\n\"","43945","44947","\"## 12. 5× / 10× Feasibility\\n\"","44970","47329","\"## 13. Monitoring Plan\\n\"","47378","48303","\"## 14. Final Classification & Conditional Action\\n\"","48348","56075","\"## 15. Sources, Assumptions & Open Questions\\n\"","\"filename\"","\"format\"","\"content_sha256\"","\"audit_evidence.json\"","\"f3028b70ddd9198a9f401690585dae27a366ed3eab242eab3868125c1b2d54e8\"","\"Complete JSON content\"","\"9e512fc92a2c601